---
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { EvidenceLabel } from "../../components/EvidenceLabel";
import { RelationshipKey } from "../../components/RelationshipKey";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteName } from "../../lib/domain";

const site = siteName();
---

<Layout
  title={`How we handle evidence — ${site}`}
  description="What Documented, Likely, Disputed and Unverified mean on Gustale, and what Associated with, Resembles and Influenced mean.">
  <Breadcrumbs
    crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { label: 'How we handle evidence' }]}
  />

  <article class="about-page inner evidence-page">
    <h1 class="about-page h1">How we handle evidence</h1>

    <p class="text-lg mb-8">
      Every claim on Gustale carries a label saying how well it is supported.
      Every connection between two things carries a mark saying what kind of
      connection it is. This page explains both, once, so you do not have to
      guess what a badge means.
    </p>

    <h2 class="about-page h2">The four evidence labels</h2>

    <p class="mb-6">
      The label belongs to a single claim or a single connection. It never
      belongs to a dish as a whole. A dish can have a well-documented name, a
      likely history and an unverified origin, and each of those is labelled
      on its own.
    </p>

    <ul class="evidence-page__labels">
      <li>
        <EvidenceLabel
          subject="claim"
          evidenceStatus="evidenced"
          hasSource={true}
          withMeaning
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <EvidenceLabel
          subject="claim"
          evidenceStatus="provisional"
          hasSource={true}
          withMeaning
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <EvidenceLabel
          subject="claim"
          evidenceStatus="evidenced"
          disputeState="disputed"
          withMeaning
        />
      </li>
      <li>
        <EvidenceLabel
          subject="claim"
          evidenceStatus="unevidenced"
          hasSource={false}
          withMeaning
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="about-page h2">The three relationships</h2>

    <p class="mb-6">
      Three kinds of connection appear on Gustale. They are not
      interchangeable, and the mark tells you which one you are looking at.
    </p>

    <RelationshipKey>
      <a href="/about/evidence">The full method, explained once.</a>
    </RelationshipKey>

    <h2 class="about-page h2">Things we do not do</h2>

    <ul class="evidence-page__rules">
      <li>
        <strong>No dish has an "Origin" field.</strong> An origin claim is a
        claim, and it carries a label like any other.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The earliest surviving reference is not an origin.</strong> We
        show it as the earliest record found, never as the place a dish began.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Resemblance never implies descent.</strong> Two dishes can look
        alike because they were made independently. We say so, and we do not
        draw an arrow.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A map position is not a claim.</strong> Where a dish is plotted
        on the map does not make the plot a historical assertion.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Classification is not ancestry.</strong> A dish's family says
        what shape it has. It does not say where it came from.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>When sources conflict, we show the conflict.</strong> We do not
        pick a winner in the summary.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="about-page h2">Who checks this</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Every published claim says who verified it and when. Anyone can propose a
      correction, and a proposed claim has to name its source. Agent-written
      claims enter as Unverified drafts with their source candidates attached;
      they are never published as findings.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .evidence-page__labels {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .evidence-page__table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .evidence-page__table th,
  .evidence-page__table td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 0.85rem 0.75rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .evidence-page__table thead th {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sub);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .evidence-page__table tbody th {
    font-family: var(--body);
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .evidence-page__rules {
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .evidence-page__table,
    .evidence-page__table tbody,
    .evidence-page__table tr,
    .evidence-page__table td,
    .evidence-page__table th {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
    }
    .evidence-page__table thead {
      display: none;
    }
    .evidence-page__table tbody th {
      white-space: normal;
      border-bottom: 0;
      padding-bottom: 0.15rem;
    }
    .evidence-page__table tbody td {
      border-bottom: 0;
      padding-top: 0.15rem;
      padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }
  }
</style>
